// std.io `prompt` + `stdin_all` (CLI-completion slice 2). `io.prompt(msg)` is the single interactive
// path that survives batch-captured output: on `RealHost` it writes `msg` to the real terminal NOW
// (bypassing the batch buffer) and reads one line; in the deterministic sandbox it writes nothing
// observable and returns the next scripted stdin line — so both backends agree (the prompt text never
// reaches the compared buffers). `io.stdin_all()` then drains the REST of stdin to EOF as one string
// (here the two remaining fixture lines, joined by a newline → two physical stdout lines).
// expect: stdout "prompted: line one"
// expect: stdout "line two"
// expect: stdout "line three"
// expect: exit 0
use std.io

// `prompt` consumes the first scripted line; its message is not observable in the sandbox.
name = io.prompt("your name? ") ?? "<eof>"
echo "prompted: ${name}"

// `stdin_all` drains everything left ("line two\nline three").
echo io.stdin_all()
